0..77 Comment "// A conditional, `if c { t } else { e }`: the case of its condition over the"
78..152 Comment "// two booleans, the true branch first. The condition is a computation the"
153..231 Comment "// case binds, as `while` binds its own, and each branch is a block whose last"
232..305 Comment "// computation is the conditional\'s answer. The derived form is the usual"
306..381 Comment "// one: `if` as the eliminator of the booleans (Levy, \"Call-By-Push-Value\","
382..450 Comment "// Springer 2003, § 2.3, where the case of a sum is a computation)."
